# AGENTS.md — externalized repository memory (FREECC template)

> Why this file exists (evidence E3, E9): every fresh agent pays full price to
> re-explore a repository ("each agent's entry into the repository, paid in full
> before anything is produced"), and long contexts are used U-shaped — the
> middle gets lost. The fix is NOT a bigger context window; it is this file:
> a small, structured, verified memory that every agent (Claude Code, OpenCode,
> mikoshi roles) reads FIRST. The ten markers below match mikoshi-construct's
> discovery protocol exactly, so `construct doctor` can mechanically check that
> they are filled (evidence E19). Fill them via `/construct-discover` or by hand.

## 1. product
<!-- construct-discover:product -->
What this product does, for whom, and where a defect costs the most.

## 2. module-map
<!-- construct-discover:module-map -->
Directory → responsibility table. One owner per concept.

## 3. commands
<!-- construct-discover:commands -->
The exact commands: install, test, lint, build, run, harness (`pnpm run quality`).

## 4. composition-roots
<!-- construct-discover:composition-roots -->
Where the system is wired together (entrypoints, DI, config loading).

## 5. dependency-policy
<!-- construct-discover:dependency-policy -->
Allowed dependency directions; enforced by lint (architecture/checklists.md).

## 6. high-effort-areas
<!-- construct-discover:high-effort-areas -->
Modules where the ladder should start at medium/high: concurrency, money,
security, schema migrations, anything with a history of repeated failures.

## 7. composition
<!-- construct-discover:composition -->
One composition model per real flow (architecture/composition/*.yaml);
diagrams are rendered from these and checked against code.

## 8. security-invariants
<!-- construct-discover:security-invariants -->
| Invariant | Enforced by |
|-----------|-------------|
| no committed secrets | gitleaks in .github/workflows/security.yml |

## 9. defects-vs-variance
<!-- construct-discover:defects-vs-variance -->
What must be treated as a defect (fails CI) vs acceptable variance (documented).

## 10. open-questions
<!-- construct-discover:open-questions -->
Known unknowns. An implementer that hits one reports `blocked` with a precise
question instead of guessing (evidence E2: a bad brief cost 4.16M tokens once).

---
### Budget discipline for agents working in this repo (FREECC policy)
1. Start every task at the LOWEST rung the task class allows (mikoshi ladder E2).
2. Never self-report success — the harness agent/verifier decides (E2, E8).
3. Read this file before exploring; update markers you discover to be wrong.
4. If context grows past ~50% of the model window, stop and write findings into
   this file or a task note; do NOT rely on the model remembering (E9).
